[6.976, "o", "      fix 0002 [bool-typedef] src/MQTTPacket.h defines its own `bool`, but on QNX 8.0 <sys/socket.h> already includes <stdbool.h> (via io-sock/types_fbsd.h), so `bool` is taken. The typedef is skipped\r\n"]
[13.432, "o", "      round 3: 35 error(s); first: /home/chirag/qnx800/host/linux/x86_64/usr/bin/x86_64-pc-nto-qnx8.0.0-ld: ../src/libpaho-mqtt3c.so.1.3.14: undefined reference to `recv'\r\n"]
[13.433, "o", "      fix 0003 [link-libsocket] `recv` is in QNX's libsocket, not in libc as on Linux: link with -lsocket.\r\n"]
[13.434, "o", "      fix 0004 [endian-netbyte] `be32toh` comes from glibc's <endian.h>, which QNX 8.0 does not have. QNX has the same names as BSD macros in <net/netbyte.h>; a small header (-included in every compil\r\n"]
