[22.049, "o", "Subject: [qnx-porter 0002] bool-typedef\r\nSource: deterministic rule\r\nReason: src/MQTTPacket.h defines its own `bool`, but on QNX 8.0 <sys/socket.h> already includes <stdbool.h> (via io-sock/types_fbsd.h), so\r\nError: /tmp/qnx-porter-demo/paho.mqtt.c/work/src/src/MQTTPacket.h:31:22: error: two or more data types in declaration specifiers\r\n---\r\ndiff --git a/src/MQTTPacket.h b/src/MQTTPacket.h\r\nindex fd384ae..ecdae83 100644\r\n--- a/src/MQTTPacket.h\r\n+++ b/src/MQTTPacket.h\r\n@@ -28,7 +28,9 @@\r\n #include \"LinkedList.h\"\r\n #include \"Clients.h\"\r\n \r\n+#ifndef __bool_true_false_are_defined  /* qnx-porter: QNX's <sys/socket.h> includes <stdbool.h> */\r\n typedef unsigned int bool;\r\n+#endif\r\n typedef void* (*pf)(int, unsigned char, char*, size_t);\r\n \r\n #include \"MQTTProperties.h\"\r\n"]
